{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["כי, פתך, באזני — [verses 7–9] three joined words." "<b>שער</b> — a past verb from מאה שערים, meaning: in a man he sets a measure in himself, to say to you: \"Eat and drink\" — so he does." "<b>ולבו בל עמך</b> — that he does not love you when you eat his bread."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:18.227085537Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}